<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Semicon holds initial public offering.</title>
<headline>LG Semicon holds initial public offering.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean LG Semicon, a unit of the LG Group, is scheduled to hold its initial public offering on Wednesday and Thursday, brokers said.</p>
<p>The semiconductor maker is offering 10 million shares at 20,000 won per share. It plans to publicly list them on October 9, lead manager Hyundai Securities said.</p>
<p>Brokers said the listing of LG Semicon could heighten fears of an oversupply of shares on the market.</p>
<p>Margin loans are at record levels of 2.74 trillion won, while customer deposits at brokerages have lagged at 2.4 trillion.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
